 Democrats"], "rationale": "Benson holds a steady 5-8 point lead across high-quality pollsters, outspends James on air, and markets and raters alike treat her as a clear but not certain favorite. The evidence supports a Likely D rating with a margin near 7 points.", "watch": "A strong closing debate performance by James or a late national environment shift toward Republicans could tighten the race into Lean D territory.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Gretchen Whitmer (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Michigan's open governor's race pits Democrat Jocelyn Benson against Republican John James after two terms of Gretchen Whitmer, who is term-limited. Polling since late September consistently shows Benson ahead, with margins ranging from about 3 to 17 points and recent averages near 7. She has also raised roughly twice as much money as James and holds a large cash advantage, while reporting indicates pro-James advertising has dropped off sharply.\n\nExpert raters broadly place the race in the Lean D to Likely D column, and prediction markets give Benson roughly a 90-95 percent chance of winning. James has sought distance from Trump in debates and pressed education issues, but has yet to close the gap. The race remains a clear but not guaranteed Democratic favorite heading into the final stretch.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9339, "margin": 7.39}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9166, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9224, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9193, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8901, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9053, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.911, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9221, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9131, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9322, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.912, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9